Dear Jim,

Thanks a lot for your reply!

If I understand your last statement well, if I want to use colext with season as a observation covariate (in obsCov) and force it the occupancy to be the same in both seasons (psi1 = psi2) than I have to compute the likelihood myself, correct?
I see in your code for occupancy that you used season as a site covariate, hence each site is actually present in 2 row in the matrix (once for season 1, and once for season 2). Is this supposed to produce different results that using 1row per site and season as an observation covariate (as I was planning to do)?

The other question is why do you add a 0 in the formula such as in  fm2 = occu(~ 0 + season ~ 1, ufo) ? I do know about the -1 to remove the intercept, but never seen a 0 before.

Best,
Stephanie

On Tuesday, 5 December 2017 21:12:56 UTC+2, Jim Baldwin, USDA Forest Service wrote:

> OK.  I put my reading glasses on.
>
> I still argue that colext will likely more appropriately give results to calculate the standard error of the difference of the two detection probabilities as it explicitly takes into account the repeated measures on each site.  Here is some code (modified from the previous message) that will obtain estimates using colext and occu.  I chose parameters psi1, epsilon, and gamma such that psi1 = psi2 to match your closure assumption in the data generation process.  First the results, then the code:
>
> # From colext:  p1 = 0.2481847; p2 = 0.5180173; p1 - p2 = -0.2698326; se(p1-p2) = 0.07919375
> # From occu  :  p1 = 0.2626047; p2 = 0.5152182; p1 - p2 = -0.2526136; se(p1-p2) = 0.06362796
>
>
> > # Generate some data with 124 sites
> > M <- 124 # Number of sites
> > J <- 3 # num secondary sample periods
> > T <- 2 # num primary sample periods
> > psi <- rep(NA, T) # Occupancy probability
> > muZ <- z <- array(dim = c(M, T)) # Expected and realized occurrence
> > y <- array(NA, dim = c(M, J, T)) # Detection histories
> > set.seed(13973)
> >
> > # Set some values for psi1, phi, and gamma such that psi1 = psi2
> > psi[1] <- 0.4 # Initial occupancy probability
> > p <- c(0.3,0.5)
> > phi <- 0.9 # Survival probability (1-epsilon)
> > gamma <-  1/15 # Colonization probability
> >
> > # Generate latent states of occurrence
> > # First year
> > z[,1] <- rbinom(M, 1, psi[1]) # Initial occupancy state
> > # Later years
> > for(i in 1:M){ # Loop over sites
> > for(k in 2:T){ # Loop over years
> > muZ[k] <- z[i, k-1]*phi[k-1] + (1-z[i, k-1])*gamma[k-1]
> > z[i,k] <- rbinom(1, 1, muZ[k])
> > }
> > }
> > # Generate detection/non-detection data
> > for(i in 1:M){
> > for(k in 1:T){
> > prob <- z[i,k] * p[k]
> > for(j in 1:J){
> > y[i,j,k] <- rbinom(1, 1, prob)
> > }
> > }
> > }
> >
> > # colext analysis
> > yy <- matrix(y, M, J*T)
> > season <- matrix(c('01','02'),
> > nrow(yy), T, byrow=TRUE)
> > simUMF <- unmarkedMultFrame(y = yy,
> >   yearlySiteCovs = list(season = year), numPrimary=T)
> > fm = colext(~1, ~1, ~1, ~ 0 + season, simUMF)
> > # Brute force transformation of parameter estimates
> > detection.probs = 1 - 1/(1+exp(fm@estimates@estimates$det@estimates))
> >
> > # occu analysis
> > y2 = rbind(y[,,1],y[,,2])
> > site.covs2 = data.frame(season = c(rep("Season 1",M),rep("Season 2",M)))
> > ufo = unmarkedFrameOccu(y = y2, siteCovs = site.covs2)
> > fm2 = occu(~ 0 + season ~ 1, ufo)
> > detection2.probs = 1 - 1/(1+exp(fm2@estimates@estimates$det@estimates))
> >
> > # Summary
> > cat("From colext:  p1 = ",detection.probs[1], " p2 = ",detection.probs[2],"\n")
> >
> > cat("From occu: p1 = ",detection2.probs[1], " p2 = ",detection2.probs[2],"\n")
> >
> > # Comparing standard errors of the difference between estimates of p1 and p2
> > # From colext
> > v = fm@estimates@estimates$det@covMat
> > p1 = detection.probs[1]
> > p2 = detection.probs[2]
> > # Using delta method
> > se.diff = ((-1 + p1)*p1*((-1 + p1)*p1*v[1,1] - 2*(-1 + p2)*p2*v[1,2]) +
> >   (-1 + p2)**2*p2**2*v[2,2])^0.5
