If the true values of the colonization and extinction probabilities are extremely low, then that would result in very few changes of site status.  So if the observed status is pretty much the same in each year for each site, then it wouldn't be surprising to get such low values.  Does observed status stay the same at a site from year to year?

If there are many changes in status over time, then I think we'd need to see your data to go any farther.

Jim

